---
/**
 * Terms of service — public page; doubles as the EULA URL Intuit's
 * production review asks for.
 */
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Terms of Service · Pocket Ops</title>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-900">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 p-6 pb-16">
      <header class="pt-6">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-700">← Pocket Ops</a>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">Effective 6 July 2026</p>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The service</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Pocket Ops provides customer management, quoting, invoicing, payments, messaging,
          and accounting-sync tools for UK field-service businesses. By creating a workspace
          you accept these terms on behalf of your business.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Your account and your data</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          <li>You are responsible for keeping your login credentials secure and for the activity of users you invite to your workspace.</li>
          <li><strong>Your data stays yours.</strong> Customer records, jobs, invoices, documents, and messages belong to your business; we process them only to provide the service (see the <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a>).</li>
          <li>You must have a lawful basis to store your customers' details and to message them; you agree not to use messaging features for unsolicited marketing (spam).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Payments and third-party services</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Card payments are provided by Stripe under your own Stripe account and Stripe's
          terms; Pocket Ops never holds your funds. Connections to Stripe, Twilio, Google,
          and QuickBooks are optional, governed by those providers' terms,
          and can be disconnected by you at any time. Subscription fees, where applicable,
          are billed in advance and are non-refundable except as required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Acceptable use and availability</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Don't misuse the service: no unlawful content, no attempting to access other
          workspaces' data, no interfering with the platform's operation. We aim for high
          availability but the service is provided "as is" without warranty; to the maximum
          extent permitted by law our total liability is limited to the fees you paid in the
          twelve months before a claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot
          lawfully be limited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Ending the agreement</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          You can close your workspace at any time; we may suspend or terminate workspaces
          that breach these terms. On closure we delete your data as described in the Privacy
          Policy. These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="text-center text-xs text-zinc-400">
        <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a> · © 2026 Pocket Ops ·
        <a href="mailto:support@pocketops.io" class="underline">support@pocketops.io</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
